possible for the  same person to become  conservator of both the estate and the  person to be appointed as both  separate petitions have to be filed so  what is the legal standard to  force another adult person into a  conservatorship  well california probate code section  1821 requires the initial petition to  show the following number one  the inability of the proposed  conservative to properly provide for his  or her needs for physical health food  clothing and shelter  two the location of the proposed  conservatives residents and the ability  of the proposed conservative to live  in the residence while under  conservatorship three  alternatives to conservatorship  considered by the petitioner  or proposed conservator and reasons why  those alternatives are not available  number four health and social services  provided to the proposed conservative  during the year preceding the filing of  the petition  and number five the inability of the  proposed conservative to substantially  manage his or her own financial  resources  or to resist fraud or undue influence  this  is and frankly should be a very high bar  for the petitioner to clear  the facts need to show that the person  is not capable of taking care of  themselves  or of managing their own finances or  that they are susceptible to  manipulation  now in the case of britney spears we  don't know exactly what the facts were  that the court relied on when it  determined that britney needed a  conservatorship back  in 2008 when jamie spears petitioned the  probate court  britney had been through enormous  upheaval in a very short period of time  britney was harassed repeatedly by the  paparazzi she publicly shaved her head  shortly after the death of a beloved  aunt  and this event was captured by cameras  and became an enormous tabloid story  she was also in a divorce and in a  custody battle with kevin fetterline  she had voluntarily gone to rehab and  done two stints in a psychiatric  institution  we assume that she has a disability but  we don't know whether she has any  psychiatric diagnosis  now jamie spears also told the court  that britney's new manager sam lufty  was abusing her and the court in these  proceedings entered a restraining order  against  lufty now while we don't have all of  this information  i don't think anyone seriously  questioned the necessity of the spears  conservatorship  at the time however in retrospect it's  fair to ask whether the spears family  could have used a less restrictive  measure to protect brittany or  whether this conservatorship has gone on  for way too long  now what are some less restrictive  measures that could have been instituted  well  for starters a power of attorney where a  person legally authorizes an individual  to make  financial decisions for them this could  be a spouse a friend a manager or even a  lawyer  a person might also agree to give  temporary custody to their children to  their ex  giving someone power of attorney allows  them to make decisions on your behalf  but it doesn't allow them to control  your every waking moment  there can be mediations in court-ordered  rehab when drugs are an issue  and someone who has power of attorney  can create a trust and pay the bills of  their client and  put them on an allowance all of these  are serious steps but they don't compare  to the severity of  a conservatorship but of course  sometimes conservatorship  is necessary now you might ask aren't  there some legal safeguards to make sure  that the conservatorship is  necessary on a continual basis well  there are supposed to be safeguards in  these arrangements  the conservator has to periodically  report to the court about the status of  the situation in some circumstances the  conservator will need  court's approval to make certain  decisions and in the beginning of this  process a court-appointed investigator  is responsible for interviewing the  potential conservative  explaining their rights and making  recommendations to the judge  however after the conservatorship is  established the investigator only speaks  to the conservative  every two years and here jamie spears  maintained full control over brittany  even after sam lufty was gone her  divorce and custody arrangements were  final  and her drug use had apparently ended  public reports show that  jamie quote had the authority to  restrict and limit her visitors oversee  her personal security  and dictate her medical and psychiatric  treatment jamie has repeatedly said that  he only wants what's in her best  interest and that he loves his daughter  and wouldn't force her to do anything  that she wouldn't want to do  but of course the free britney movement  has pointed out cracks in this facade  for years when britney had a successful  run of shows in las vegas  people started to question why a highly  skilled performer was still  under a conservatorship then things  started to unravel publicly in 2019.  in january jaime's original  co-conservator andrew wallett resigned  after asking for a raise  that left jaime spears as the sole  conservator of both spears's person and  estate  the new york times recently reviewed a  transcript of a hearing from the spring  of 2019 when britney's lawyer quote  asserted that she had been forced into  mental health facilities against her  will  on exaggerated grounds which she viewed  as punishment for standing up for  herself and making an objection during a  rehearsal  at the time britney's lawyer filed a  document saying that britney was afraid  of her father and  later in 2019 kevin fetterline backed up  this claim  he helped their teen sons file for a  restraining order against jamie because  of something he did  to one of their children when they  visited with jaime and  federer line's attorney said quote  britney exercised appropriate parental  conduct removing her children from a  dangerous situation  this order was granted without  opposition from jaime and barred him  from 